DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The VVFFSS__SSYYNNCC() macro writes out all unwritten data in the file system
     mounted as _m_p.

     The arguments it expects are:

     _m_p       The file system.

     _w_a_i_t_f_o_r  Whether the function should wait for I/O to complete.  Possible
              values are:

              MNT_WAIT    synchronously wait for I/O to complete

              MNT_NOWAIT  start all I/O, but do not wait for it

              MNT_LAZY    push data not written by file system syncer

     The VVFFSS__SSYYNNCC() macro calls the _v_f_s___s_y_n_c method of the file system, which
     normally calls VOP_FSYNC(9) for all the vnodes in the file system.

